1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,766
The disagreement inside the municipality was about the occupancy of a coastal lawn, and it grew out of a murder that had happened in the next village.

2
00:00:08,766 --> 00:00:25,534
“The law is strong,” the counselor said, “and the reliance of the public on a solemn policy is not a myth.” The two sides did not differ about the facts; they differed about the order in which the facts mattered.

3
00:00:25,534 --> 00:00:32,753
The residential community wanted a peaceful locality with a naval memorial and an extended lawn.

4
00:00:32,753 --> 00:00:41,012
The outside investor wanted an honorary citizenship, a charming hotel, and a noble clientele.

5
00:00:41,012 --> 00:00:45,261
“You cannot accommodate both,” the heiress said.

6
00:00:45,261 --> 00:00:52,001
“One of them will conceal the other, and the government will call it persuasion.”

7
00:00:52,001 --> 00:00:56,580
The controversy was institutional as much as social.

8
00:00:56,580 --> 00:01:04,219
“A racist clause in a private contract is still injurious to the public interest,” the observer wrote.

9
00:01:04,219 --> 00:01:17,898
“The domination of one market by one family is not economic freedom.” The beggar at the gate of the municipality had a different point of view, and no one asked him for it.

10
00:01:17,898 --> 00:01:29,911
The romantic story of the coastal estate had turned into a fictional one: a mythical founder, a murderous rival, and an alleged deception at the heart of the deed.

11
00:01:29,911 --> 00:01:34,385
“We are emphatic about the wrong thing,” Lin said.

12
00:01:34,385 --> 00:01:40,930
“The right question is who pays for the drainage, not who owns the myth.”

13
00:01:40,930 --> 00:01:48,989
The community and the state disagreed about the next step, and the disagreement was the most honest thing in the room.

14
00:01:48,989 --> 00:01:56,908
“A society that cannot say who is responsible will always look for a foreigner or a beggar,” Maya wrote.

15
00:01:56,908 --> 00:02:02,317
“That is how a supremacy of the loud becomes a policy.”

16
00:02:02,317 --> 00:02:07,272
The solemn conclusion of the meeting was that nothing had been decided.

17
00:02:07,272 --> 00:02:19,155
The extended lawn, the naval museum, and the honorary title stayed on the table, and the room, for once, was quiet enough to hear the sea.

18
00:02:19,155 --> 00:02:34,521
It was vain to argue about religion and money against a council that had already decided; the extended lawn and the honest question were the only things left, and the next village would hear about it either way.
